<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick Seymour</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1820">1820</a>–<a href="/years/1869">1869</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick Seymour was a British colonial official who succeeded James Douglas as governor of the mainland Colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-columbia">British Columbia</a> in 1864. After the colony was merged with Vancouver Island in 1866 he governed the united Colony of British Columbia, at a time of heavy debt from road building and falling gold output, until his death in office in 1869.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-seymour.jpg" alt="Frederick Seymour" width="303" height="543" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frederick_Seymour_Governor_of_British_Columbia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
